## Overview
This question evaluates understanding of inter-thread synchronization, producer-consumer patterns, and low-level data structure design in operating system environments.

## Key Concepts
- Circular buffer with head/tail indices and wraparound handling
- Mutexes and condition variables for blocking operations and wakeups
- Memory visibility guarantees via compiler and hardware memory barriers
- Correctness and performance characteristics with multiple concurrent producers

## Code Example
```c
typedef struct {
    char data[LOG_SIZE];
    int valid;
} slot_t;

slot_t buffer[N];
int head = 0;
int tail = 0;
int count = 0;

mutex_t mtx;
cond_t not_full;
cond_t not_empty;

void enqueue(const char *record) {
    mutex_lock(&mtx);
    while (count >= N)
        cond_wait(&not_full, &mtx);
    buffer[tail % N] = *(slot_t *)record;
    tail++;
    count++;
    cond_signal(&not_empty);
    mutex_unlock(&mtx);
}

void dequeue(char *record) {
    mutex_lock(&mtx);
    while (count == 0)
        cond_wait(&not_empty, &mtx);
    *(slot_t *)record = buffer[head % N];
    head++;
    count--;
    cond_signal(&not_full);
    mutex_unlock(&mtx);
}
```

## Test Plan
1. **Correctness**: Verify no data loss or corruption with single producer/consumer
2. **Blocking**: Confirm enqueue blocks when buffer is full, dequeue blocks when empty
3. **Throughput**: Measure records/second with 1, 4, 8, and 16 concurrent producers
4. **Stress**: Run sustained test to detect race conditions and memory leaks

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason about live-code updates in a running kernel, including synchronization, cache coherence, and control of instruction fetch paths under contention.

## Key Concepts

- Live patching of executable memory without stopping workers
- Per-page state machines and atomic publish
- I-cache/TLB synchronization and rollback safety

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal C-like sketch (pseudo-code)
enum { STABLE, STAGED, ACTIVE } state_t;
typedef struct { void *addr; void *code; state_t s; volatile int refcnt; uint64_t ver; } page_t;

int publish_patch(page_t *p, void *new_code) {
  p->s = STAGED;
  p->code = new_code;
  __sync_synchronize();
  if (atomic_compare_exchange(&p->s, STAGED, ACTIVE)) {
    atomic_fetch_add(&p->ver, 1);
    icache_invalidate(p->addr, PAGE_SIZE);
    tlb_invalidate(p->addr, PAGE_SIZE);
    return 0;
  }
  return -1;
}
```

